The machine boundary of the linked ARM English ledgers
=====================================================

Scope and evidence
------------------
specimens.tsv binds the two original binaries and listings by commit and
SHA-256. They are GNU/Linux EABI softfp and hardfp specimens, not physical
Android-device evidence. readelf ABI flags and attributes distinguish them.
The annotated object and linked copies remain separate occurrences.

Bytes in ledger headers are in increasing memory-address order. The original
GNU A32 word e92d4008 therefore appears as 08402de9. Thumb f04f 0b00 appears
as 4ff0000b. The original assembly column remains unchanged, including comments.

Register and execution obligations
----------------------------------
General registers R0-R15 are 32 bits. SL/R10, FP/R11, IP/R12, SP/R13, LR/R14 and
PC/R15 denote aliases. VFP D registers have 64-bit payloads and overlap their
corresponding S-register pairs; exact access/alias effects remain unverified.
Printed register lists and the implicit following register in A32 LDRD/STRD
require full expansion before a complete state transformer is certified.

An A32 word occupies four bytes. T32 instructions in the hardfp startup region
occupy either two or four. A sequential successor is address plus encoded width;
it is not the value read as PC and does not assert that the instruction runs,
returns normally, has permission, or has that successor after a branch or fault.
A32 ordinary PC operands generally use address plus eight. Thumb ordinary PC
operands generally use address plus four; literal loads/address-generation forms
can align that value. Exact operand/encoding rules remain verification work.

A32 condition evidence is read from the encoding's condition field. The
preliminary predicates describe APSR.NZCV; S spellings request encoding-specific
flag updates. No universal preservation of the other flags is claimed. Thumb
startup has no printed IT instruction, but arbitrary incoming ITSTATE and entry
paths are unknown. The ledger preserves that context obligation. CBZ/CBNZ and
conditional branches have their separate predicate behavior.

BL, BLX, BX, POP containing PC, LDM containing PC and ordinary PC writes need
different control-flow rules. BL/BLX write LR; immediate BLX crosses instruction
states in these captures. Indirect values, state changes, target permissions,
return addresses, exceptions and actual execution-index changes remain
uncertified. A direct target printed as a PLT name is a captured stub, not the
uncaptured library implementation.

Memory and floating-point obligations
--------------------------------------
Every memory instruction needs exact effective-address formation, source/dest
width, alignment and endianness rules, base writeback, register overlap rules,
access ordering, permissions, memory type and fault/partial-completion behavior.
Multiple transfers do not gain an atomicity guarantee from a compact sentence.
No processor memory configuration or process mappings have been captured here.

VFP payload transfers are distinct from arithmetic and conversions. Comparisons
write FPSCR.NZCV; the observed VMRS APSR_nzcv,FPSCR transfers those condition bits
to integer status. FPSCR rounding, default-NaN handling, signaling/quiet NaNs,
signed zero, denormals/flush-to-zero, accumulated flags, trapping and exact
intermediate rounding remain unverified for each form. VMLA/VMLS are not silently
treated as fused arithmetic. No host JavaScript arithmetic is used as an oracle.

ABI and external effects
-------------------------
The softfp/base and hardfp/VFP parameter conventions are separate contracts.
R0-R3/stack argument placement, callee-saved general/VFP registers, stack
alignment, by-reference Fortran arguments, return conventions and exceptional
exits all remain obligations at each call boundary. Library interface names do
not establish those libraries' actual effects. Softfp embeds five reference
BLAS bodies; dynamic dependencies, loader resolution, indirect target state,
libc behavior and missing R-side machinery retain their original unknowns.

Status discipline
------------------
All operation explanations are PRELIMINARY/ANNOTATED_ONLY. Independent byte,
mode, width, order, ABI identity and range assertions are structural evidence.
They do not certify the prose's complete meaning. Join the native_record to the
frozen semantic-forms table for explicit per-form unknowns. No form becomes
COMPLETE by gaining a ledger row. Contradictions discovered later must remain
visible alongside both the earlier explanation and its correction.

